    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, we need to find the volume of the cube with edge length six inches. To do this, we can use the formula for the volume of a cube: V = s^3, where s is the length of one edge.\nPlugging in the given value of six inches for s, we get V = 6^3 = 216 cubic inches.\nNext, we need to find the volume of the cube with edge length one foot. Since there are 12 inches in one foot, we can find the length of one edge by dividing 12 by 6: 1 foot = 12 inches / 6 = 2 inches.\nUsing the same volume formula for cubes, we get V = 2^3 = 8 cubic inches.\nFinally, we need to find the ratio of the two volumes. To do this, we divide the volume of the smaller cube by the volume of the larger cube: 8 / 216 = 1 / 27.\nTherefore, the ratio of the volume of the cube with an edge length of six inches to the volume of the cube with an edge length of one foot is 1 / 27.The answer is: 27",
