    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the ratio of the volume of a cube with an edge length of six inches to the volume of a cube with an edge length of one foot, we start by determining the volume of each cube.\n\n1. **Calculate the length of the edge of the larger cube in inches:**\n   \\[\n   1 \\text{ foot} = 12 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the volume of the larger cube:**\n   The volume \\( V \\) of a cube with edge length \\( s \\) is given by \\( s^3 \\).\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{large}} = (12 \\text{ inches})^3 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the volume of the smaller cube with edge length 6 inches:**\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{small}} = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the ratio of the volume of the larger cube to the volume of the smaller cube:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_{\\text{large}}}{V_{\\text{small}}} = \\frac{1728}{216}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Simplify the fraction:**\n   To simplify the fraction, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1728 and 216.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1728}{216} = \\frac{216 \\times 8}{216} = 8\n   \\]\n\nSo the ratio of the volume of the larger cube to the volume of the smaller cube is \\( \\boxed{8} \\).",
